  "ownershipReview": [
    "Three source handles are opened read-only with FileShare.Read and per-file length caps before streaming hashes. Their names/lengths/hashes identify actual original inputs.",
    "Bounded diagnostic tree has one statted real pack leaf; source path is the containing directory. No fabricated slot leaf or recursive GUI enumeration.",
    "BrowserSession owns the source opening while Core catalog and preview use exact snapshot/selection identity. Factory-acquired NativeSceneInput lease transfers only after constructor succeeds; untransferred lease is released on failure.",
    "Capture awaits DisposeAsync before input rehash or any output opening. Primary capture and cleanup errors are aggregated; successful native disposal is required for receipt assertions.",
    "Failed native retirement may retain the background worker, pending resources and source lease until process exit. One-shot CLI does not retain a retry handle or claim reusable-host recovery. BrowserSession retirement releases its owner without waiting for outstanding leases.",
    "Shared PNG and receipt staging both use overwrite:false. Initial file/directory guards are advisory; final publication independently refuses replacement. The outputs are individually atomic, not transactional as a pair.",
    "If receipt fails after PNG commits, the command fails and retains the complete PNG. No cleanup deletes a possibly foreign destination.",
    "Runtime receipt has no hardcoded build/pin assertion; external exact source/assembly/pin evidence is required.",
    "Capture uses exact browser FrameCamera(bounds,1), initial appearance, static scene and sampler/key policy; it cannot attest GUI interaction, changed viewport/camera state or HWND closure."
  ],
